Source: kytensor-llm
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: kylin <liuyihu@kylinos.cn>
Build-Depends: cmake (>=3.18), tongyi-decrypt, libpciaccess-dev, debhelper-compat (= 12), gf-arise-llama-ponn (=02.00.08), ocl-icd-libopencl1
Standards-Version: 3542
Homepage: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
#Vcs-Browser: https://salsa.debian.org/debian/llama
#Vcs-Git: https://salsa.debian.org/debian/llama.git

Package: kytensor-llm
Replaces: llamacpp
Breaks: llamacpp
Conflicts: llamacpp
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Description: Inference of Meta's LLaMA model (and others) in pure C/C++
 This package contains the llama.cpp core runtime libraries.
 The main goal of llama.cpp is to enable LLM inference with minimal setup and state-of-the-art performance on a wide variety of hardware - locally and in the cloud.


Package: kytensor-llm-dev
Replaces: llamacpp-dev
Breaks: llamacpp-dev
Conflicts: llamacpp-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: kytensor-llm (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: development files for llama.cpp
 This package contains the header files to compile applications that use llama.cpp, and contains the binary files to run llama.cpp.
 The main goal of llama.cpp is to enable LLM inference with minimal setup and state-of-the-art performance on a wide variety of hardware - locally and in the cloud.


